  "default_direction": "en_to_pl",
  "note": "A2 liść · rides prep_w_loc / prep_place / past_byc. A1 already owns dom, mieszkanie, pokój, kuchnia, łazienka, sypialnia, łóżko, stół, krzesło, okno, drzwi, klucz — those are ANCHORS here, never re-taught. This pack teaches 10 new house nouns plus the locative form of six of them, and the payoff is putting a thing in a place: Komputer jest na biurku. Two shapes only: NEW noun as subject with an already-taught locative (Szafa jest w pokoju), or a taught-here locative with an entirely old subject (Mleko jest w lodówce). Locative forms of A1 rooms (kuchni, sypialni, łazience) are NOT taught anywhere yet, so no sentence uses them. meble is plural-only: it takes są, never jest, and no plural past (były) exists in the pool. Nouns carry gender badges; the w/na phrases do not, since a phrase has no citation gender to teach.",
